lesson: 62
title: The number just before, just after and in between
stars: 0
explain: The number just after a number is one more; the number just before it is one less.
explain: When two numbers have exactly one number between them, that number is one more than the smaller and one less than the bigger.
explain: Between 46 and 48 is 47, because 46 + 1 = 47 and 48 - 1 = 47.
vars: a=name b=name n=10..98
answer: n + 1
exercise: {a} lives at number {n} and {b} lives at number {n+2}. One house stands between them. What is its number?
exercise: Seat {n} and seat {n+2} are taken. {a} sits in the seat between them. What is the number of {a}'s seat?
exercise: {a} thinks of the number just before {n+2}. What number is it?
exercise: {b} thinks of the number just after {n}. What number is it?
exercise: Page {n} and page {n+2} are torn. Which page number is in between?
exercise: On a number line, {a} marks {n} and {b} marks {n+2}. Which number lies between the two marks?
test: Which whole number sits between {n} and {n+2} on the number line?
test: The locker after number {n} belongs to {a}. What is the number on {a}'s locker?
test: {b}'s ticket is one less than {n+2}. What number is on the ticket?
test: Counting from {n} to {n+2}, {a} says one number in the middle. Which one?
exercise: Which number comes right after {n}?
exercise: What number is one more than {n}?
exercise: On a bus in Melbourne, {a} sits in seat {n+2} and {b} sits in seat {n}. Which seat number lies between them?
exercise: {a} counts {n}, then says the next number. What does {a.he} say?
exercise: What number is one less than {n+2}?
exercise: Room {n} and room {n+2} are in a school in Cork. Which room number is between them?
exercise: A tram in Auckland is at stop number {n}. What is the number of the very next stop?
exercise: Between {n} and {n+2} there is one whole number. What is it?
test: Name the whole number that is bigger than {n} by exactly one.
test: {a} reaches {n} while counting beads, then counts one more bead. What number does {a.he} say for that bead?
test: {b} has the raffle ticket right before ticket {n+2}. What number is {b}'s ticket?
test: What do you get when you take one away from {n+2}?
test: The mailboxes in a New Jersey building are numbered in order. Box {n+2} is two boxes after box {n}. What number is on the box between them?
test: Which is the one number sitting between {n+2} and {n}?
exercise: {a}'s at number {n}, {b}'s at {n+2}, whats the house in between
exercise: seat {n+3} — no wait, {n+2} — and seat {n} r taken. which seat's in the middle
exercise: whats after {n}? quick
exercise: {b} says the number between {n} and {n+2} is {n+2}. nah, which is it really
test: number before {n+2} pls, my nan's 80 and she forgot lol
test: locker after {n} is mine, whats my number then
test: pages {n} n {n+2} torn out, which one's missing between em
exam: Determine the integer which lies strictly between {n} and {n+2}.
exam: It is given that the dwellings numbered {n} and {n+2} are separated by precisely one dwelling. State the number of the intervening dwelling.
exam: Identify the integer which immediately succeeds {n.words} in the conventional order of counting.
exam: Ascertain the integer which immediately precedes {n+2}, given that {a} and {b} occupy seats {n} and {n+2} respectively.
exercise: The late Mrs Bell lived at number {n} and {b}'s nan, who passed away last year, lived at number {n+2}. {a} lives in the house between them. What is {a}'s house number?
exercise: Grandad was laid to rest in plot {n}, and Grandma in plot {n+2}. Their old dog was buried in the plot between them. What is that plot's number?
test: {b} says the number between {n} and {n+2} is {n+2}. with the greatest respect, mate, that's crap — what is it really
